+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static homepage with client-side WebMCP tools. No backend or payment processing is included. Order drafts exist only in memory and reset on reload.
+
+## Browser tools
+
+The page feature-detects `document.modelContext.registerTool`, with a fallback to the older `navigator.modelContext.registerTool`. In browsers without WebMCP, the order form and drink buttons still work.
+
+| Tool | Input | Effect |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `get_seasonal_menu` | `{}` | Returns the displayed Seasonal Favorites menu, including drink IDs, names, descriptions, and details URLs. |
+| `order_drink` | `{"drinkId":"maple-oat-latte","quantity":2}` | Adds to the visible local order draft and scrolls to the order panel. Quantity defaults to 1; each drink is limited to 10 per draft. |
+| `highlight_drink` | `{"drinkId":"cold-brew"}` | Highlights, focuses, and scrolls to the chosen drink card. |
+
+Drink IDs are `maple-oat-latte`, `dark-roast-espresso`, and `cold-brew`. The menu is read from the page rather than maintained as a second list. Tool results include text content and structured data; invalid inputs return `isError: true` with an actionable error and do not change the order.
+
+The registration API follows the [WebMCP specification](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/). Browser support is experimental and requires a compatible browser configuration.
+
+## Checks
+
+Run `npm test` for Node-based tests with a DOM test double. They cover registration, shared manual and agent ordering, input validation, highlighting, and operation without WebMCP. Run `node --check webmcp.js` for a syntax check. No build step is required for this static site.
